  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nAn upper level low continues to spin just east of the area\nacross the Hudson Valley and Catskills. In fact, the low is\nretrograding a bit to the west, which has allowed showers and\nthunderstorms to pivot back into the area, especially across\nCentral NY. These showers and thunderstorms will produce brief\nheavy downpours and may result in localized poor drainage/urban\nflooding. Flash flooding is unlikely, but cannot be completely\nruled out if thunderstorms were to train over the same areas.\nFortunately the axis of heavier rainfall is west of the hardest\nhit areas from yesterday/last night (Sullivan and Delaware\ncounties). However, we will need to watch those counties closely\nas it won't take much additional rainfall to cause renewed\nflooding issues.\n\nScattered showers will continue overnight and into Thursday as \nthe low pressure system slowly drifts east. That being said, the\nthreat for locally heavy rainfall will be diminishing\nsignificantly.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nThe above mentioned low pressure system will finally move far\nenough east of the region to keep conditions dry on Friday as\nsurface high pressure and weak upper level ridging moves in.\nThis will result in much-needed dry weather for Friday and \nSaturday. With the weak ridging and sunshine, temperatures will\nbe warmer with highs mainly in the upper 70s to mid 80s.\n\nThe second half of the weekend become a bit more uncertain. A weak \nsurface low pressure will develop over the lower Mississippi River \nValley Saturday and it drifts eastward. With high pressure over the \nAtlantic and this low near the Ohio River Valley, flow around these \nsystems will advect moisture northward leading to showers developing \nSunday. A frontal system then passes through late Sunday into Monday \nkeeping rain around early next week. Model guidance diverge on what \nhappens after the front moves through. Solutions like the ECMWF keep \nan upper level low present and the high pressure closer to the coast \nwith rain showers on Tuesday. Other solutions like the GFS have a \ntrough and dry northwest flow over the region. Given the \nuncertainty, chances for showers are forecasted Sunday through \nTuesday with the highest chances on Sunday.",
